The approach relies on `setCameraLimits` with radius limits to hold the distance inside the range, and on `attachControl` for mouse, wheel, and pinch input. I have not verified these points, since the library isn't available here:

- The declarations don't say whether `setCameraLimits` clamps radius on every frame, including while inertia is still moving the camera. If it only clamps on input, the zoom range is not guaranteed.
- I assumed `attachControl` and `setCameraLimits` are exported from the package root `@babylonjs/lite`. They are declared in `arc-rotate-controls.d.ts`, so the import path may need changing.
- I assumed the returned dispose function from `setCameraLimits` removes its per-frame work, and that calling it doesn't leave the other limits altered. I also assumed `attachControl` with default options handles pinch and enables keyboard controls in the way you expect.
